<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">August 12, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 166 of Operation Epic Fury</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-08-12T07:12:00Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v48.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      Hormuz framework talks stall on accumulated pre-conditions from both sides with no signed interim text in hand (<span class="cite">F1</span>); formal US–Iran sessions absent since April as Iran's new IRGC-veteran security chief replaces the official associated with corridor negotiations (<span class="cite">F2</span>).
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">4 active · last reasoned 2026-08-12 · 7 resolved this cycle (F1–F7 prev.)</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">NEAR-TERM (≤72h)</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today.</div>

      <!-- 7–30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F1</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US and Iran publicly announce a signed interim Hormuz commercial-shipping framework agreement before EOD 2026-08-19?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">25%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp (initial · 2026-08-12)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-19</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Oman channel reached an 'advanced stage' August 4–6 with geographic corridor coordinates circulating between parties (Axios, 5 Aug; Al Jazeera, 6 Aug). But on August 8 Araghchi stated a reopening is 'subject to other conditions' including US redress for alleged MOU violations (CNN, 8 Aug). On August 10 Trump publicly demanded unspecified 'compensation' from Iran before talks can advance (CNN, 10 Aug) — a new condition absent from earlier drafts. Iran's parliament simultaneously reviewing a competing harder 10-point framework. Three conditions must converge within 7 days for YES; historical base rate for 'near-deal' claims converting to a signed instrument within 7 days: low.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if publicly confirmed signed interim Hormuz framework announced by both governments (or named mediator readout of mutually acknowledged signed text) before EOD 2026-08-19. Unilateral declarations without counterpart confirmation = NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/CNN/Axios/Al Jazeera) plus US State Dept or Iranian MFA/IRNA confirming the same instrument.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Agreed-in-principle without signed text = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Iran parliament passes rival 10-point proposal without US acceptance = NO. One side announces, other denies within 24h = NO unless both clarify.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Oman FM signed-text readout</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump withdraws compensation demand</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran MFA accepts corridor text without added conditions</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F2</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a TIER1-confirmed formally convened US–Iran negotiating session (direct or Oman/Qatar/Pakistan-mediated) occur before EOD 2026-08-26?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">35%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp (initial · 2026-08-12)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-26</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Qatar FM confirmed August 4 that the region is 'fully engaged' but no direct talks are scheduled (Euronews, 4 Aug). Oman's role as primary channel expanded in recent weeks (CNN, 4 Aug). However, Iran's new national security chief — an IRGC veteran appointed around August 10–11 — made public statements before appointment expressing skepticism toward formal US-Iran talks (US News/NBC, 7 Aug). Trump's August 10 compensation demand and Iran's August 8 MOU-violation claim add pre-conditions absent from earlier frameworks. Last formally convened round: Islamabad talks, April 11–12. Oman channel relays draft texts; it has not hosted a formal session.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if TIER1 reports a face-to-face or formally convened indirect negotiating session between named US principals (Witkoff or equivalent) and named Iranian principals (Araghchi or equivalent), hosted by a named mediator (Oman/Qatar/Pakistan), before EOD 2026-08-26.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters/AP/AFP/Axios/CNN/Al Jazeera plus US State Dept or Iran MFA/IRNA confirmation of the same session.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Relay of written messages or draft texts without a named convened session = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Unilateral 'talks continue' without mediator or counterpart confirmation = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Oman FM convenes named session with readout</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran new security chief endorses formal engagement</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump withdraws Aug 10 compensation demand</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30–90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 DAYS</div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F3</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Hormuz commercial transit volume reach ≥40 vessels/day (7-day moving average) before EOD 2026-09-30?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">25%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp (initial · 2026-08-12)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-30</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Lloyd's List Intelligence (5 Aug brief) recorded 84 commercial transits July 27–August 2 = approximately 12 per day. Pre-crisis baseline: approximately 94 per day. Reaching ≥40 per day within 49 days requires a signed Hormuz framework (F1), MCM progress sufficient for JMIC SUBSTANTIAL-to-MODERATE downgrade, and Lloyd's P&I war-risk cover reinstatement. MCM with LCS platforms and Knifefish UUVs is active but no CENTCOM cleared-corridor declaration has been issued. JMIC downgraded from SEVERE to SUBSTANTIAL (August 5) — first movement, but far from MODERATE. Stacked dependencies against the tight timeline.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IMF PortWatch or equivalent AIS aggregator records ≥40 commercial transits/day averaged over any consecutive 7-day window before EOD 2026-09-30.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Lloyd's List Intelligence Hormuz Brief plus one of: IMF PortWatch, Bloomberg shipping, or Reuters/AP/AFP shipping report confirming the same 7-day average.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Military vessels excluded from commercial count. Navy-escorted commercial convoys count. Sources diverging by more than 20% = flag AMBIGUOUS. Single-day surges without qualifying 7-day average = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Lloyd's records 7-day avg ≥25 transits/day</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">JMIC downgrades to MODERATE</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Lloyd's P&I war-risk cover reinstated</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">F4</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US and Iran publicly sign a comprehensive peace/nuclear framework agreement covering nuclear enrichment limits, Hormuz freedom of navigation, and a sanctions roadmap before EOD 2026-10-27?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">25%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">Δ 0pp (initial · 2026-08-12)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-27</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">The June 17 MOU established a 60-day framework that broke down in early July when Iran struck commercial vessels (Arms Control Association, July 2026). A comprehensive agreement requires resolution of enrichment caps, sanctions architecture, Hormuz governance, and reconstruction financing. New pre-conditions from both sides (US compensation demand August 10; Iran MOU-violation claim August 8) have stalled even the intermediate Hormuz-only step. Iran's new IRGC-veteran security chief and parliament's competing harder framework are structural obstacles. Israel's October 27 election creates partial Trump political incentive to demonstrate diplomatic progress before year-end. p=0.25 reflects the narrow but non-trivial path through the stacked obstacles.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if publicly confirmed signed comprehensive agreement jointly announced by both governments, covering all three domains: (1) Iran nuclear enrichment limits or elimination; (2) Hormuz freedom of navigation guarantee; (3) US sanctions relief roadmap — before EOD 2026-10-27.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>US State Dept and Iran MFA/IRNA joint or simultaneous announcement plus two TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/CNN) confirming all three domains covered.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Hormuz-only deal without nuclear/sanctions = NO. Nuclear-only without Hormuz = NO. Agreed-in-principle without signed text = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. MOU extension without new nuclear commitments = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">F2 (formal session) resolves YES</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">F1 (interim deal) signed and holds ≥2 weeks</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran accepts zero/cap-enrichment as negotiating basis</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 6–12 MONTHS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">6–12 MONTHS</div>
      <div class="forecast-empty-slot">No publishable forecast in this horizon today.</div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24–48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>On August 10, President Trump publicly stated that the United States requires unspecified "compensation" from Iran before Hormuz talks can advance (CNN, 10 Aug). Two days earlier, Foreign Minister Araghchi had declared a reopening "subject to other conditions" including US redress for alleged MOU violations (CNN, 8 Aug). The accumulated new pre-conditions meant the Oman channel as of August 12 continued relaying draft texts without a signed instrument; Araghchi had told Al Jazeera on August 2 that negotiations were "in final stages," a characterization neither confirmed nor updated by either government in the August 10–12 window. → moved <span class="cite">F1</span></p>

      <p>Around August 10–11, Mojtaba Khamenei conducted a six-position restructuring of senior military and security leadership (US News/NBC, 7 Aug). The new national security chief — an IRGC veteran — replaced the official previously publicly associated with Hormuz framework negotiations. Pre-appointment public statements attributed to the incoming chief included skepticism toward formal US-Iran talks. Iran's hard-line factions had openly opposed the June 17 MOU after its signing, and the restructuring aligns with Mojtaba Khamenei's circle consolidating security command across the military-intelligence apparatus (NCRI, 11 Aug). → moved <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>Lloyd's List Intelligence (5 Aug brief) recorded 84 commercial transits during July 27–August 2 — approximately 12 per day — a substantive recovery from near-zero levels during the April–May blockade, but still 87 percent below the pre-crisis baseline of approximately 94 per day. JMIC simultaneously downgraded the Hormuz threat level from SEVERE to SUBSTANTIAL, the first downgrade since the crisis began, citing IRGC maritime behavior as "less volatile" in the post-MOU period. US mine-countermeasure operations with LCS platforms and Knifefish UUVs were active per the August 5 Lloyd's brief, but no CENTCOM clearance for a swept corridor had been issued, and Lloyd's war-risk premiums remained at levels precluding normal P&I commercial scheduling. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>

      <p>NCRI (11 Aug) documented pensioner protests in Tehran, Mashhad, Kermanshah, and Shush focused on hyperinflation and an upcoming fuel-price adjustment, with chemotherapy costs reported at ten times their 2024 levels. The same brief reported that Mojtaba Khamenei's faction issued a formal warning to President Pezeshkian against accepting his own resignation — the latest in a documented series of 28 such resignation-threat episodes — and that Pezeshkian's public response was his IRNA statement of August 2: "If we have survived to this day, it is thanks to Iran's noble people." The IRGC apparatus and Mojtaba's circle hold de facto control over security and military decisions; Pezeshkian's civilian mandate over economic policy remains contested and unresolved as of August 12. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>Israeli election campaigning proceeded without major domestic political developments in the August 10–12 window. US News and NBC (7 Aug) reported Smotrich's Religious Zionism at seven seats in polling near or below the 3.5 percent threshold, with Netanyahu reported as likely to arrange a further right-wing electoral merger before October 27 to prevent Smotrich's parliamentary elimination. No major Israeli strikes on Iran or Iranian proxy targets beyond Lebanon-front Hezbollah containment operations were reported in the 24–48 hour window. Netanyahu's caretaker government remains formally responsible for all security decisions until the October 27 vote. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
      <span class="meta">Computed from Forecast Board · 1 sentence per scenario</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="scenario-map">
      <div class="prob-bar-container">
        <div class="prob-bar prob-escalation" style="width:40%;">Escalation 40%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-status" style="width:35%;">Protracted 35%</div>
        <div class="prob-bar prob-deescalation" style="width:25%;">De-esc 25%</div>
      </div>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path:</strong> Iran's new IRGC-veteran security chief holds the pre-condition line, no formal session occurs before August 26 (F2 resolves NO), and Hormuz remains below 20 transits/day through autumn as the comprehensive-deal track (F4) expires.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path:</strong> Oman channel produces a narrowly scoped interim Hormuz corridor deal (F1 resolves YES), transit volumes begin climbing toward the F3 threshold, but a comprehensive nuclear-sanctions framework (F4) stalls past the Israeli election date.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path:</strong> Trump withdraws the compensation demand, a formal session occurs by August 26 (F2 resolves YES), transit volume crosses 40/day by September 30 (F3 resolves YES), and a comprehensive agreement is reached before October 27 (F4 resolves YES).</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · ~200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>

      <p>Iranian state media — IRNA, Press TV, Tasnim, and Fars — maintained three consistent framing themes in the August 10–12 window. The Strait of Hormuz was presented as Iranian sovereign territory exercising legitimate administrative authority over its waters, not as an international strait under UNCLOS freedom-of-navigation rules. IRNA carried Deputy Foreign Minister Gharibabadi's characterization of the Oman framework as Iran "establishing the conditions for transit through the Islamic Republic's strategic maritime corridor" (IRNA relay, 4 Aug). Press TV described proposed transit fees as "deferred compensation for decades of free passage through Iranian waters" — framing any fee as a historical debt rather than a new demand. No state media outlet acknowledged the July 6–7 attacks on commercial vessels conducted by Iranian forces that triggered the current negotiating round. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>The August 10–11 military leadership restructuring received uniform coverage as a routine administrative event. Tasnim described the six appointments as measures "strengthening the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps' organizational resilience and command unity." The new national security chief received a brief official biography across all state platforms without reference to previously reported skepticism toward US-Iran formal talks. IRNA did not acknowledge the departure of the official previously publicly associated with Hormuz framework negotiations. No state media outlet characterized the transition as a policy shift. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>Economic vulnerability coverage in IRNA, Tasnim, and Fars attributed hyperinflation, the upcoming fuel-price adjustment, and reduced purchasing power exclusively to "the criminal sanctions siege imposed by the US and its Zionist allies." President Pezeshkian's August 2 statement — "If we have survived to this day, it is thanks to Iran's noble people" — was published in full across all three platforms and then clipped as a headline for five consecutive days. Pensioner protest coverage was absent from IRNA and Fars in the August 10–12 window; Tasnim published a brief note on August 11 attributing the gatherings to "organized enemy instigation and foreign interference in Iran's internal affairs." No state media outlet acknowledged the internal Pezeshkian-Mojtaba tension documented by NCRI. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

